## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical understanding of attention math, dimensions, scaling, and how tokenization affects token-to-token alignment in real models.

## Key Concepts

- Dot-product attention math and scaling (√d_k)
- Softmax over keys for each query
- Tokenization impact on alignment
- Practical pitfalls in batching

## Code Example

```javascript
function simpleAttention(q, k, v) {
  // q: [d], k: [n, d], v: [n, d]
  const scores = k.map(row => dot(q, row) / Math.sqrt(d));
  const weights = softmax(scores);
  return weights.reduce((acc, w, idx) => acc + w * v[idx], 0);
}
```

Why This Is Asked

This question probes how a senior engineer designs AI-driven data access with strong governance. It combines dynamic planning with real-time policy evaluation, privacy-preserving processing, and robust production observability across multi-tenant data stores.

Key Concepts

- LangChain + AutoGen planning for tool orchestration
- Runtime policy evaluation (per-user/tenant) and policy-as-code integration
- PII redaction and differential privacy for aggregations
- Auditing, tracing, and metrics for compliance and reliability
- Retry/backoff, idempotence, and observability in distributed data workflows

Code Example

